  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "IBUlDxrgdVrC9HxkjPKFhPSBLaM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:54:42.099Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "| Store | Browser | Node | Bun |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `MemoryAnalyticsStore` | \u2705 | \u2705 | \u2705 |\n| `BrowserAnalyticsStore` | \u2705 | | |\n| `KnexAnalyticsStore` | \u2705 | \u2705 | \u2705 |\n| `PostgresAnalyticsStore` | | \u2705 | \u2705 |\n\nTwo of the four have behaviour worth knowing before choosing.\n\n**`MemoryAnalyticsStore`** is in-memory by way of **a WASM build of Postgres \u2014 PGlite**. It requires an asynchronous `await store.init()` for two reasons: downloading and initialising the WASM build when no `PGlite` instance was supplied, and initialising the in-memory database's schema. The initialisation is **idempotent** (existing tables are not recreated), and \u2014 importantly \u2014 `init()` **is not on the `IAnalyticsStore` interface**, only on the concrete type, so a caller holding the interface cannot initialise it. Both `knex` and `pglite` objects can be passed in, which is how it shares a database with other consumers.\n\n**`PostgresAnalyticsStore`** uses the `pg` package and **assumes a fully-initialised Postgres database already exists** \u2014 the opposite contract. It takes a connection string or a `knex` instance, and adds a `raw(sql: string)` method that is *not* on the interface and is explicitly \"not intended for production use cases\".\n\nBoth accept the same optional constructor extras for observability: `queryLogger`, `resultsLogger` and a `profiler`.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/typescript/compatibility.md` \u2014 whole compatibility matrix\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/typescript/memory.md` \u2014 Construction; Initialization\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/typescript/pg.md` \u2014 Construction; Raw queries\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:54:42.099Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:54:42.099Z"
    }
  },
